INT. ROLLER DERBY ARENA - HOME LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Cinderblock walls painted purple. Metal lockers, dented. Skates in a heap, laces knotted. A boombox plays muffled brass from the rink upstairs.

CAPTAIN ROSALIE "ROSIE RIOT" DUARTE (30s, shoulders like a door, fishnet sleeves) paces the room with her helmet under one arm. JUNE "JUNEBUG" ABARA (20s, jammer, a half-eaten banana in her fist) sits cross-legged on a bench. COACH EZEKIEL "ZEKE" WARDELL (60s, cardigan, bad knee) props himself against a locker and consults a clipboard. BEATRIX "BIX" HOLLANDER-SINGH (40s, the team's blocker, mouthguard hung on her neck) kneels to lace a skate, while Rosie stops, looks at Junebug, looks at Zeke, and starts pacing again, and June takes a bite of banana and offers Bix the other half, which Bix waves off without lifting her eyes from her laces.

ZEKE
They're quick but they're not smart. First jam, don't engage.

ROSIE
We don't engage?

ZEKE
You hold the line. June skates.

JUNE
I skate.

ROSIE
Hold the line.

BIX
Hold the line.

ROSIE
Hold the line.

BIX ^
Hold the line.

They laugh. Zeke does not.

ZEKE
Rosie. A word.

She crosses to him. They step into the corridor. A pipe drips. He does not look at her for a while, then he takes his glasses off and rubs the bridge of his nose.

ZEKE (CONT'D)
My knee's done after tonight.

ROSIE
I know.

ZEKE
You're getting the whistle next season.

She stands very straight. Her gloved hand finds the doorframe.

ROSIE
Win first.

ZEKE
Win first.

Down the hall, the brass band reaches its finale. Bix calls from inside.

BIX (O.S.)
Captain! They're announcing us!

Rosie squares her shoulders. Zeke tucks the clipboard under his arm. Together they go in.
